 "how_to_read": "Each vector is a base instance (support form: n, checks, syndrome bits s, integer weights w, candidate cand, facets [row, F, num, den] or a tree) with ONE slot, at `path`, replaced by `value` exactly as JSON writes it (1.0 stays a float, true a bool, \"1\" a string). Adapters in tests/test_qldpc_input_domain.py carry the value into each implementation's own format untouched. Every applicable implementation must reach `expect` (the float screen `expect_screen` where given); `not_expressible` names formats with no slot for the value.",
 "provenance": "the 66-probe matrix of the adjudication of external audit 2 (2026-11-03, findings F05/F06), plus the divergences found while writing the contract: repeated candidate, F and row entries read as sets by the production checker; one-element row combinations read as single rows by tree checker B and the JavaScript tree checker; multipliers 2/2 and -1/-1 normalised by JavaScript; and (the final referee, 2026-11-03) facets with multiplier 0 skipped before validation by six of the seven implementations, flat and at tree depth 1",
